  "body": {
    "id": "prop:qmax-network-augmentation",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "Let \\(q_{\\max}=\\max_{x\\in\\mathcal X}q_x\\), and suppose the candidate menu contains \\(F\\subseteq E^+\\) with \\(r_{q_{\\max}}(E\\cup F)=q_{\\max}(|V|-1)\\).  The minimum-weight contracted-union augmentation \\(F_*\\) exists, every minimum-cost saturating augmentation has exactly\n\\[\nq_{\\max}(|V|-1)-r_{q_{\\max}}(E)\n\\]\nnew labeled edges, and \\(G+F_*\\) generically attains rank \\(q_x(|V|-1)\\) in every stratum.  Hence \\(\\ker(A_P)\\subseteq\\ker(R_0)\\) and all target root contrasts are generically identified for every compatible target latent mixture.  If the menu is infeasible at rank \\(q_{\\max}(|V|-1)\\), no permitted augmentation simultaneously saturates all proxy-effective stratum spaces.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "q_max",
      "q_x",
      "Xcal",
      "E_plus",
      "c_plus",
